-- title:
--   Transport of the Drinfeld function field along a constant-field isomorphism
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and let $k$, $k'$ be fields equipped with algebra structures over the field `GaloisField q 2` of $q^2$ elements, each such that the coordinate ring `CoordRing q k` (respectively `CoordRing q k'`) is a domain; here `CoordRing q k` is the quotient of the polynomial ring $k[X_0,X_1]$ in two variables by the ideal generated by `drinfeldPoly q k - 1`, with $x$ and $y$ the classes of $X_0$ and $X_1$. Let $e : k \simeq k'$ be an isomorphism of $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebras. The assertion is that there exists a ring isomorphism $\varphi$ between the fraction fields `drinfeldFunctionField q k` and `drinfeldFunctionField q k'` of these two coordinate rings such that: $\varphi$ restricted to the constants agrees with $e$, i.e. $\varphi(\iota(a)) = \iota'(e\,a)$ for all $a \in k$, where $\iota,\iota'$ are the structure maps of $k$, $k'$ into the respective fraction fields; $\varphi$ carries the image of $x$ to the image of $x$ and the image of $y$ to the image of $y$; and $\varphi$ is equivariant for the action `hFunctionFieldAction`, namely $\varphi(h \cdot f) = h \cdot \varphi(f)$ for every $f$ and every $h$ in `hSubgroup q`, the kernel of the character $(g,\alpha) \mapsto \det(g)\,\alpha^{q+1}$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/q) \times \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^{\times}$, acting on each fraction field by the extension to fractions of the automorphisms `hAction` of the coordinate ring. Note that $\varphi$ is asserted only as an isomorphism of rings, its behaviour on constants being pinned down by the first clause rather than by an algebra structure.
--
--   This is the base-change statement for the Drinfeld curve $xy^q - x^qy = 1$ of Deligne–Lusztig along an isomorphism of the constant field over $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$, in a form compatible with the action of the group $H$ of pairs $(g,\alpha)$ with $\det(g)\alpha^{q+1} = 1$. It is used to transport the associated $\ell$-adic data, in [`DrinfeldCurve.exists_linearEquiv_tateProd_comp_tateProdRep_eq_of_algEquiv`](thm.html#DrinfeldCurve.exists_linearEquiv_tateProd_comp_tateProdRep_eq_of_algEquiv), from one constant field to another.
